<p class="text-badge font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Key Takeaways</p>
<p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4 speakable">Anker alternatives for OEM buyers: four routes, MOQ 500 to 3,000+, 65W GaN FOB $6.00-8.50 and a 7-point supplier scorecard. Compare before you quote.</p>
<ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
<li>Anker sells under its own brand and does not offer a public private-label program. An "Anker alternative" is a sourcing route, not a rival logo.</li>
<li>The four routes differ sharply: authorized distribution sets MOQ by agreement but gives no brand control; ODM stock private label starts at 500 units; ODM design development at 1,000–2,000; full OEM with new tooling at 3,000+.</li>
<li>The 2025 recall shows why cell traceability and change-control clauses matter more than brand reputation. CPSC recorded 19 reports of overheating, fire or explosion in one US recall alone.</li>
<li>A 65W multi-port GaN charger costs $6.00–8.50 FOB at 500 units. Landed cost, channel margin and certification amortization decide whether a private label program works.</li>
<li>Use a seven-point supplier scorecard with pass/fail thresholds. A supplier that cannot document cell model, AQL and aging data is not an Anker-class partner.</li>
</ul>
