<h3 class="text-lg font-black text-brandBlue mt-6 mb-3">6.1 What to put in the supply contract</h3>
<ol class="list-decimal pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-600 mb-4"><li>1. <strong>Cell model and supplier in the purchase order.</strong> No substitution without written approval.</li><li>2. <strong>Change notification.</strong> Advance notice before any cell, IC or housing change.</li><li>3. <strong>Batch traceability.</strong> Each carton maps to a cell lot and production date.</li><li>4. <strong>Indemnity.</strong> The supplier carries recall and replacement cost for unauthorized changes.</li><li>5. <strong>Retained samples.</strong> Keep signed golden samples for each batch.</li></ol>
<h3 class="text-lg font-black text-brandBlue mt-6 mb-3">6.2 Anker-Level Supplier Scorecard: Seven Pass/Fail Checks</h3>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl mb-6"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden"><thead><tr class="bg-brandBlue text-white text-badge font-black uppercase tracking-widest"><th class="p-4 text-left">#</th><th class="p-4 text-left">Check</th><th class="p-4 text-left">Pass threshold</th><th class="p-4 text-left">Fail signal</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-slate-600"><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">1</td><td class="p-4">Factory identity</td><td class="p-4">Legal entity, USCC or registration number, site address</td><td class="p-4">Only a trading company name</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">2</td><td class="p-4">Certification scope</td><td class="p-4">Certificate names the exact model and cell</td><td class="p-4">"Similar model" coverage</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">3</td><td class="p-4">Cell traceability</td><td class="p-4">Cell model, supplier and lot on record</td><td class="p-4">"Grade A" with no datasheet</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">4</td><td class="p-4">Aging test</td><td class="p-4">100% 4-hour aging, with logs</td><td class="p-4">Batch sampling only</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">5</td><td class="p-4">AQL and defect data</td><td class="p-4">AQL 0.65 normal / 0.25 tightened; defect rate below 0.3%</td><td class="p-4">AQL quoted only as a buyer target</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">6</td><td class="p-4">Change control</td><td class="p-4">Written approval clause</td><td class="p-4">Verbal assurance</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">7</td><td class="p-4">Audit access</td><td class="p-4">Live video or on-site audit allowed</td><td class="p-4">Refuses process walkthrough</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">A supplier that passes all seven is worth a premium. A supplier that fails two or more is a recall risk, regardless of price.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">For the full audit sequence, use our <a href="/blog/choose-reliable-china-charger-supplier/">China charger supplier verification guide</a> and the <a href="/blog/on-site-factory-audit-checklist-china-charger-oem/">on-site factory audit checklist</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="cost-model-factory-fob-vs-brand-distribution" class="mb-16">
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
<div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">7. Cost Model: Factory FOB vs Brand Distribution</h2>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">The FOB price is only the first line. Build the full model before you choose a route.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Illustrative example: 65W multi-port GaN charger, 500 units</strong></p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl mb-6"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden"><thead><tr class="bg-brandBlue text-white text-badge font-black uppercase tracking-widest"><th class="p-4 text-left">Line</th><th class="p-4 text-left">Low case</th><th class="p-4 text-left">High case</th></tr></thead><tbody class="text-slate-600"><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">FOB Shenzhen</td><td class="p-4">$6.00</td><td class="p-4">$8.50</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">Freight, insurance and packaging</td><td class="p-4">$0.60</td><td class="p-4">$1.10</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">Duty and import fees</td><td class="p-4">Apply your market rate</td><td class="p-4">Apply your market rate</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">Certification amortization ($2,500–4,500 ÷ 500 units)</td><td class="p-4">$5.00</td><td class="p-4">$9.00</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4"><strong>Landed cost before duty</strong></td><td class="p-4"><strong>$11.60</strong></td><td class="p-4"><strong>$18.60</strong></td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4">Wholesale price at 40% retailer margin on a $39.99 retail price</td><td class="p-4">$24.00</td><td class="p-4">$24.00</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-slate-100"><td class="p-4"><strong>Gross margin before duty and marketing</strong></td><td class="p-4"><strong>$12.40</strong></td><td class="p-4"><strong>$5.40</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">The certification line is the one buyers most often omit. At 500 units a $2,500–4,500 package adds $5.00–9.00 per unit, not cents. The program still clears $5.40–12.40 per unit before duty and marketing, but the high case leaves little room for returns. At 1,000–2,000 units the same package falls to $1.25–4.50 per unit. The numbers are illustrative.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Build your own model with the <a href="/blog/import-costs-guide/">import cost and duty guide</a>, which covers HS 8504.40, HS 8507.60 and the landed-cost formula.</p>
<h3 class="text-lg font-black text-brandBlue mt-6 mb-3">7.1 What the model changes about your route</h3>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Authorized distribution has a different math. You buy at a distributor price and sell at retail. The margin is thinner, but you carry less certification and inventory risk. For a retailer testing demand, that can be the right trade.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">For certification cost and timing, our <a href="/blog/certifications-us-eu-guide/">certification guide for US and EU importers</a> lists the standard packages. A CE/FCC/RoHS package with UN38.3 typically runs $2,500–4,500 and takes 4–6 weeks.</p>
<blockquote class="border-l-4 border-brandOrange pl-4 italic text-slate-600 mb-4"><strong>EXPERT INSIGHT</strong>  "A buyer should never compare FOB quotes without normalizing what is included. Ask whether the quote covers Grade-A cells, the aging test, certification documents and retail packaging. A $1 difference per unit usually means one of those four items was removed."  — Nina Nico, Global Procurement & Sourcing Manager at WOWOHCOOL, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/nico-power-bank-chargers" target="_blank" rel="noopener external">LinkedIn</a></blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="conclusion-choose-the-route-before-the-supplier" class="mb-16">
<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
<div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">Conclusion: Choose the Route Before the Supplier</h2>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Anker alternatives for OEM buyers are not another logo. They are four routes with different economics.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">If you need stock now, distribution is fastest. If you need your own brand with limited risk, start with 500 units of ODM stock. If you need differentiation, move to platform design. If you need exclusivity, budget for full OEM tooling.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">Whichever route you choose, verify the cell, the certificate scope and the change-control clause. The 2025 recall is a reminder that brand reputation does not replace supplier evidence.</p>
<p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong>Ready to compare a factory quote against your target retail price?</strong> <a href="/service/">Start your OEM project</a>. We will send a line-item quote that separates product, certification and packaging, so you can compare it with any other supplier.</p>
